              },
              "question": "<p>Which of the following is correct about Selective Serotonin Reuptake Inhibitors (SSRIs)?</p>\n"
            },
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "metadata": {
              "contentType": "Multiple Choice",
              "license": "U",
              "title": "Untitled Multiple Choice"
            },
            "subContentId": "2053668e-3a5d-4304-a0a4-c19bd7f5344d"
          },
          {
            "params": {
              "media": {
                "disableImageZooming": false
              },
              "answers": [
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>Amitriptyline is a relatively common example of TCAs that has been found to be useful in chronic pain, neuropathic pain, and fibromyalgia.&nbsp;</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "They generally have some antimuscarinic actions resulting in side effects including dry mouth, blurred vision, constipation\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "They generally have antihistamine effects resulting in side effects including mental confusion and sedation\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>TCA's generally have some antiadrenergic activity resulting in side effects including postural hypotension.</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>No, if they are taken <strong>at night</strong>, the side effects of postural hypotension, and mental confusion (etc) are not as much of an issue.&nbsp;</div>\n",
                    "tip": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": "<div>Your answer was correct; if they are taken <strong>at night</strong>, the side effects of postural hypotension, and mental confusion (etc) are not as much of an issue.&nbsp;</div>\n"
                  },
                  "text": "<div>TCA's are generally recommended to take in the morning.&nbsp;</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>No, there are now Serotonin and Noradrenaline Reuptake Inhibitors (S<strong>N</strong>RIs) that generally have fewer side effects and block both.&nbsp;</div>\n",
                    "notChosenFeedback": "<div>Your answer was correct, there are now Serotonin and Noradrenaline Reuptake Inhibitors (S<strong>N</strong>RIs) that generally have fewer side effects and block both.&nbsp;</div>\n",
                    "tip": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>TCAs are the only antidepressant that significantly blocks BOTH the reuptake of serotonin AND noradrenaline</div>\n"
                }
              ],
